        "## Node Description (JSONObjectIteratorNode)\nThis Node iterates through key-value pairs in a JSON object.\nInput:\n- json_input: JSON object string\n- index: Starting index\n- mode: fixed/incr/decr iteration mode\nOutput:\n- key: Current key\n- value: Current value\n- current_index: Current position\n- total_items: Total pairs\n## Exception\n- ValueError if input is not valid JSON object\n## Multi Workflow\nIf you use this node in severval workflows at the same time, they will use the same index. Like, workflow1 get index 1, then run workflow2, workflow2 will get index 2 not index 1(because index 1 is got by workflow1)"
